        <h3>Worth checking on-site</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg> The exact leash rule is not confirmed by our sources for this communal trail — check on-site or keep your dog on a leash as a precaution.</li>
          <li><svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg> Official wildfire risk dates (prefectural order no. 2025-101 of 13/05/2025, Alpes-Maritimes prefecture): heightened vigilance from 1 June to 30 September; fire and smoking banned in natural areas from 1 July to 30 September; access to forested areas may be closed around midday from mid-June to mid-September depending on the daily risk level (map at risque-prevention-incendie.fr/alpes-maritimes).</li>
          <li><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg> A "no dogs" sign without a legal basis (municipal/prefectural order) has no binding legal value — but is still worth heeding out of courtesy.</li>
          <li><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg> Follow the GR5/GR51 markers, then the yellow markers towards the fort.</li>
